<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anacreon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 582–c. 485 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Anacreon was a Greek lyric poet from Teos in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ionia">Ionia</a>, famous for short songs about love and wine. When the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persians">Persians</a> conquered Ionia he joined the Teians who founded Abdera in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thrace">Thrace</a>, and later lived at the courts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polycrates">Polycrates of Samos</a> and of the Peisistratids in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a>. Later imitations of his style, the Anacreontea, influenced European poetry for centuries.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anacreon.jpg" alt="Anacreon" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Eric Gaba (Sting) · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anacreon_Louvre.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>His court attracted the poets <b>Anacreon</b> and Ibycus and the physician Democedes of Croton, and he made alliances first with Amasis of Egypt and later with Cambyses II of Persia.</blockquote><a href="/empire/samos">Samos · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Anacreon</b>, the lyric poet, was born there.</blockquote><a href="/state/teos">Teos</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Teos, in what is now <a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a>. Died in Teos, in what is now <a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=38.18,26.79&amp;year=-519" aria-label="Teos on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5217 792 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Anacreon"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5667 1062h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5667 1062h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=38.18,26.79&amp;year=-519">What was here in 519 BCE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
